{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>The length of one.</b> The word אחת is anomalous, for it ought to be אחדת, since the dalet is not among the servant letters [i.e., letters serving as matres lectionis]; only because two letters, dalet and tav, were joined, both of the same origin, it is burdensome for the tongue — in the manner of משָרַת את המלך (1 Kings 1:15) — and the dalet was dropped."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The phrase 'מאותיות המשרתים' ('servant letters') refers to matres lectionis; resolved by context from Ibn Ezra's grammatical terminology."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:33.236140510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}